{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Ra'ukha</b> — According to R. Moses' view: that this alludes to the time when HaShem drove the sea with a fierce east wind. And in my view: that it speaks of the time when 'the sea returned toward morning,' for 'in the sea' refers to the time on behalf of Israel, as I have explained the reason for 'and the Israelites walked on dry land' — since it says [it] twice; and likewise from the Song it is the verse: 'For Pharaoh's horse came.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 77, :notes {0 "The lemma 'ראוך' appears to be an abbreviated/corrupt form; translated hyper-literally as written. The phrase 'לאומרו פעמים' is elliptical; rendered as 'since it says [it] twice,' following the apparent sense that the verse repeats a form."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:50.979682011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}